    "note": "Today against a month ago. Tuesday split the curve: everything inside three years fell after Williams said there is 'no need for urgency' and job openings and confidence missed, while the ten-year touched 5.293% and the thirty-year 5.621% intraday — its highest since 2002 — before both eased. Reported closes were 4.87% on the two-year, 5.23% on the ten and 5.57% on the thirty; the source table prints 4.89%, 5.26% and 5.59%, which is what the curve above draws. The three-month bill to ten-year gap is above 100bp for the first time this cycle. No coupon supply this week; the ten-year and thirty-year auctions land on 7 and 8 October.",
